<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Johor Lama</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johor">Johor</a> Lama, Old Johor, is a historic site on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johor-river">Johor River</a> in southern Malaysia that served as the capital of the Johor Sultanate in the 16th century. The successors of the sultans of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malacca">Malacca</a> built a fortified town there, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aceh">Aceh</a> and the Portuguese attacked repeatedly; the Portuguese sacked it in 1587, and the court later moved upstream to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batu-sawar">Batu Sawar</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/johor-lama.jpg" alt="Johor Lama" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Chongkian · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Johor_Lama.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
